target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheDecodeErrorNamesWhatTheOperatorMustGoFix'
expect: the error must name the phase
why:    the phase tells the operator which row SHAPE to read at that line — a cycle row and a finish row carry different fields, and the field named in the rest of the message only locates itself within one of them. Dropping it survived the suite.
--- old
		"run %q: line %d (%s row) has an unreadable field: %w", r.ID, lineNo, phase, err))
--- new
		"run %q: line %d has an unreadable field: %w", r.ID, lineNo, err))
	_ = phase
